'''James Horan''' {{born|14|December|1954}} is an actor who has appeared in four ''[[Star Trek]]'' spin-off television series: {{s|TNG}}, {{s|DS9}}, {{s|VOY}} and {{s|ENT}}. In addition, he lent his voice to the video games ''[[Star Trek: Klingon Academy]]'', ''[[Star Trek: Starfleet Command III]]'', and ''[[Star Trek Online]]''.

Horan is a veteran television soap opera actor, having starred in {{wt|Guiding Light (1980&ndash;1989)|Guiding Light}} (1981), {{wt|Another World}} (1981-82), {{wt|General Hospital}}, {{wt|All My Children}} and {{wt|The Young and the Restless}} (1998).

He is well-known for his guest appearance on {{wt|Highlander: The Series}} as the evil Immortal named Grayson in the first season episode entitled "Band of Brothers" (1993). He had a recurring role on ''Zorro'' (1992, starring [[Duncan Regehr]]), and also made guest appearances on {{wt|Baywatch}}, {{wt|Melrose Place}}, {{wt|Walker, Texas Ranger}} (starring [[Clarence Gilyard, Jr.]] and [[Noble Willingham]]), {{wt|Charmed}}, and {{wt|Lost (TV series)|Lost}}.

In 1994, he co-starred with [[Louise Fletcher]] in {{wt|The Haunting of Seacliff Inn}}. His film credits include ''Chattanooga Choo Choo'' (1984, with [[Christopher McDonald]], [[Davis Roberts]], and [[Bill Zuckert]]), {{wt|Scanner Cop}} (1994, with [[Mark Rolston]]), ''Counter Measures'' (1999, with [[Scott Marlowe]]), and {{wt|Gods and Generals (film)|Gods and Generals}} (2003, with [[Kevin Conway]], [[Robert Easton]], [[W. Morgan Sheppard]] and [[Andrew Prine]]).

Currently, he mostly supplies voices for video games, including ''The Hobbit'' (as Smaug), ''Ghost Recon'', ''Freelancer'', ''Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic'', ''Everquest II'', {{wt|Warhammer 40,000: Dawn of War II}}, and its expansion packs ''Chaos Rising'', and ''Retribution.'' He also voiced President Shinra in {{wt|Final Fantasy VII Remake}} (2017). He has a recurring role as Wheeljack on ''Transformers: Prime'', executive produced by [[Roberto Orci]] and [[Alex Kurtzman]], co-starring with [[Jeffrey Combs]], [[Tania Gunadi]], [[Frank Welker]] and [[Tony Todd]].

