'''Kathryn A. "Kitty" Swink''' {{born|22|October|1954}} is an actress who played Minister [[Rozahn]] in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 2|second season]] episode {{e|Sanctuary}} and [[Luaran]] in the [[DS9 Season 7|seventh season]] episode {{e|Tacking Into the Wind}}. She also provided the voice of Luaran in the {{video game}} ''[[Star Trek: Deep Space Nine - The Fallen]]''.

Swink has been married to ''Deep Space Nine'' regular [[Armin Shimerman]] since 1981.

Swink commented, "''I grew up watching [[TOS]] with my oldest brother, who went on to become a rocket scientist. He was always going to be a scientist, but ''Trek'' put his head in the stars.''" {{el|warpfactortrek.com/an-interview-with-kitty-swink}}

Swink has guest starred in ''[[Babylon 5]]'' (1995, starring [[Claudia Christian]], [[Bill Mumy]], [[Andreas Katsulas]] and [[Tucker Smallwood]]), {{wt|The Agency (2001 TV series)|The Agency}} (2001, with [[David Clennon]], [[Ronny Cox]], and [[Heidi Schultz]]), {{wt|Becker (TV series)|Becker}} (2002, with [[Terry Farrell]]), {{wt|NYPD Blue}} (2004, starring [[Gordon Clapp]], with [[Dennis Christopher]] and [[Richard Herd]]), {{wt|Monk (TV series)|Monk}} (2007, starring [[Ted Levine]]), and {{wt|Crossing Jordan}} (2007, starring [[Miguel Ferrer]] and [[Jerry O'Connell]]), and {{wt|Leverage (American TV series)|Leverage}} (2009, with [[Brent Spiner]], Armin Shimerman, and directed by [[Jonathan Frakes]]).

She became a SAG Health Plan Trustee along with [[William Schallert]] and [[Barry Gordon]]. Swink, like Schallert, Gordon and [[Joseph Ruskin]] served on the Screen Actors Guild Executive Board of Directors and then became a Trustee at the Screen Actors Guild Pension and Health Plan.

In the early 2000s, Swink was diagnosed with pancreatic cancer. She survived and now works to raise awareness about the illness through the {{w|Pancreatic Cancer Action Network}} (PanCAN). In {{y|2024}}, she appeared on the {{s|TT}} episode {{p|PanCAN PurpleStride with Kitty Swink, Armin Shimerman, and John Billingsley}}, where she talked about the organization.

