'''William Dennis Hunt''' {{born|1|March|1944|died|14|June|2020}} who appeared as [[Huraga]] in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 4|fourth season]] episode {{e|The Way of the Warrior}}.

Hunt's other television credits include {{wt|L.A. Law}} (1992, starring [[Corbin Bernsen]] and [[Larry Drake]], with [[Amy Benedict]] and [[Timothy Carhart]]), {{wt|Wings (1990 TV series)|Wings}} (1994, starring [[Steven Weber]]), ''[[Babylon 5]]'' (1995, starring [[Claudia Christian]] [[Bill Mumy]] and [[Andreas Katsulas]]), ''[[Frasier]]'' (1998, starring [[Kelsey Grammer]]), ''Seven Days'' (2000, with [[Norman Lloyd]] and [[Alan Scarfe]]), [[J.J. Abrams]]' {{wt|Alias (TV series)|Alias}} (2003, starring [[Merrin Dungey]] and [[Victor Garber]], with [[Christian Slater]], [[L.L. Ginter]], [[Tracy Middendorf]] and [[Terry O'Quinn]]), {{wt|Modern Family}} (2013, starring [[Ariel Winter]]) and a recurring role as Judge Edgar Byrnes on {{wt|NYPD Blue}} (2003, with [[Daniel Benzali]] and [[Don Stark]]).

His first film role was Emperor Wang the Perverted in {{wt|Flesh Gordon}} (1974, with [[John Hoyt]]). He later appeared in {{wt|Flesh Gordon Meets the Cosmic Cheerleaders}} (1989).

Other film credits include {{wt|Critters 3}} (1991, with [[Bill Zuckert]], and [[Geoffrey Blake]]), ''Peephole'' (1992, with [[Jerome Butler]], [[John Short]], and [[Laura Cameron]]), {{wt|Chaplin (film)|Chaplin}} (1992), ''Lightning in a Bottle'' (1993, with [[Don Stark]], [[Matt McCoy]], [[Julianna McCarthy]], and [[Scott Marlowe]]), {{wt|Dr. Giggles}} (1992, written and directed by [[Manny Coto]], with [[Larry Drake]], [[Cliff DeYoung]], [[John Vickery]] and [[Patrick Cronin]]), and {{wt|Dragonfly (2002 film)|Dragonfly}} (2002, starring [[Joe Morton]] and [[Kathy Bates]], with [[Susanna Thompson]], [[Lisa Banes]], [[Casey Biggs]], [[Leslie Hope]], [[David Doty]], [[Jerome Butler]], [[Joseph Will]], [[Lise Simms]], [[Paul Terrell Clayton]], [[Heidi Swedberg]], [[Nicholas Cascone]], [[Samantha Smith]], [[Gillian Vigman]] and [[Jennifer S. Parsons]]).

Hunt [[Star Trek deaths#June|passed away]] on 14 June 2020 at the age of 76. {{el|abouttheartists.com/artists/484634-william-dennis-hunt}}

